{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>At Mount Sinai.</b> Everywhere it says 'at Mount Sinai' — it was said on the mountain before his descent, in Tishrei. And this passage too was said on the day after the giving of the Ten Commandments. And the reason these passages were written here in the book of Torat Kohanim is because they contain the commandments of sabbatical years and jubilees, which involve the priests — as it is written, ״והעברת שופר תרועה״ etc., and it is written, ״ובני אהרן יתקעו״ etc., and they contain the commandments of herem-dedications, which belong to the priests, and valuations, which the priests assess. Here Rashi explained: since we do not find that the sabbatical of lands was repeated in the plains of Moab, etc. — that is, after the passage of the Hebrew slave was said here and repeated in Deuteronomy in the portion of Re'eh, this sabbatical of lands was not repeated there. We learn — perforce — that its general principles and its specifics were stated from Sinai. If so, 'at Mount Sinai' here is superfluous. Rather, come and learn from here — concerning every single utterance that was spoken to Moses — such as the rest of the commandments, and all matters of sabbatical years, and even the passage of the Hebrew slave — that from Sinai were their general principles and their specifics and their fine points, and they were repeated in the plains of Moab — as we find the passage of the Hebrew slave, which was stated here and repeated in the plains of Moab."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:05.210318965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}